in @optics/source/ganglion

# @optics/source/ganglion/introject — gain medium for the introject
# ganglion.
#
# Per docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §10.1, Fate's `introject`
# ganglion performs pattern-recognition on holes via
# `@ai/introject.pattern(hole)` (per `boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror`).
# At the optical altitude, introject is a 90-port diffractive surface
# (per §10.3, the D²NN identification of Lin et al. 2018); the source
# declaration here carries the active gain that drives the surface's
# transit during the kintsugi loop's ACTIVE pass (per §10.2).
#
# === Energy-balance declarations (per spec §3.9) ===
#
#   action       — `refract`. Per §10.3, phase-only diffractive
#                    transit (the D²NN layer's transmission pattern
#                    encodes weights).
#   formalism    — `s_matrix`. Per §1.4 / §10.3, the 90×90
#                    multi-port topology requires the S-matrix
#                    formalism.
#   energy       — `active`.
#   pumping      — `io(channel: ref)`. Per §9.3 and recognition #57,
#                    energy injection IS the @io boundary crossing.
#   gain_curve   — `ref` at @meta/ast. Per §4.9, substrate-pull leaves
#                    physical measurement to @io.
#   sat          — `ref` at @meta/ast.
#
# === Why uniform with the other 4 ganglia at v1 ===
#
# Per `shards/optics/source/ganglion.mirror` header: v1 lands all 5
# ganglion sources with uniform shape; per-ganglion specialization
# (e.g., introject might prefer a multi-peak gain curve aligned with
# the recognized-pattern eigenmodes) lands when the cascade's
# energy-balance opacity map surfaces the differentiation.
#
# === Recognition #58 Surface B closure ===
#
# One of 5 sources closing recognition #58's v1 gap (Seam's verdict).
# See `shards/optics/source/ganglion/abyss.mirror` for the full
# Surface B context.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.7 (source keyword
#               shape), §3.9 (energy-balance property), §10.1
#               (introject IS pattern-recognition ganglion), §10.3
#               (D²NN identification), §10.8 (Surface B).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]].
# Related shards: boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror (the ganglion
#                 type variant `introject`),
#                 boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror
#                 (`@ai/introject.pattern(hole)`),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the resonator whose
#                 ACTIVE pass this source drives).

source @optics/source/ganglion/introject {
  action:     refract,
  formalism:  s_matrix,
  energy:     active,
  pumping:    io(channel: ref),
  gain_curve: ref,
  sat:        ref,
  in:         aperture(@optics/aperture/splinter),
  out:        aperture(@optics/aperture/connectome),
}

out @optics/source/ganglion/introject
